    "turn_text": "I know what it is. I mean, I stay in touch with some of my former Republican colleagues, and I will give them crap. You know, I'll text them. And, you know, I'll send, you know, I send them Christmas cards and I know they're, you know, I ask them about their families and I know them and we joke and stuff like that. I got along pretty well with my colleagues, I thought. And I will just chide them and basically say, why can't you just come out and say the election that Biden won the election? And they'll be blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah. And ultimately comes down to, I'd lose my primary. That's what it comes down to. I finally get them to say that. And these guys, I understand they want to be senators. And they want to stay in power. And they want to be senators. And each of them has different, I mean, Lindsey Graham, of course, went from just hating Trump to playing golf with them. And he just wants Lindsey wants to be part of the action. He also wanted to get reelected in South Carolina. He wants to be in the game. And I think that's his whole life, basically. And that's kind of it. It's great to be Senator.",
